# Stages

Purpose:
  Stage definitions for the SDDRA chain graph. Each stage represents
  a distinct phase in the development lifecycle with specific inputs,
  outputs, and approval gates.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @AN.sdd (Analyze)
   3 @AR.sdd (Architecture)
   4 @DB.sdd (Database)
   5 @BE.sdd (Backend)
   6 @API.sdd (API)
   7 @FE.sdd (Frontend)
   8 @MD.sdd (Mobile)
   9 @QA.sdd (Quality Assurance)
   10 @SC.sdd (Security)
   11 @TS.sdd (Testing)
   12 @DO.sdd (DevOps)
   13 @RV.sdd (Review)
   14 @VR.sdd (Verification)

Rules:
  [ST1] Every stage MUST have a defined input and output contract.
  [ST2] Stages MUST NOT be skipped without explicit approval.
  [ST3] Stage transitions MUST be recorded in state.

